# Sephiroth, Fabled SOLDIER: "Whenever Sephiroth enters or attacks, you may sacrifice another creature. If you do, draw a
# card." Bot1 casts an Ornithopter, then Sephiroth (Mox Jet, Ruby, Pearl), and sacrifices the Ornithopter as he enters: a card
# is drawn (the third Ornithopter) and the sacrifice is a creature dying, so his other ability drains 1 (Bot2 19, Bot1 21). That is the first resolution
# of the turn. On turn 3 (a new count) Bot1 makes an Ornithopter, Bot2 has two, and Pyroclasm kills all three: three
# resolutions are not four, so Sephiroth stays the front face, no emblem (Bot2 16, Bot1 24). Turn 3 then attacks: he may
# sacrifice another creature, and Bot1 declines (the empty answer): nothing is drawn, and his 3 damage leaves Bot2 at 13.

